;; L9 slice 2 -- aif. The AUTHORING lane for the rationale layer, second pilot
;; section.
;;
;; war-room (slice 1) is the section where the harvest found nothing: 27
;; measured absences, zero corroborated relations. aif is the opposite case --
;; 33 patterns, 62 attestations, no absence rows at all, the section
;; P-organise-the-library calls best-attested. So this slice asks a question
;; slice 1 could not: in the section where @why edges DID earn attestations,
;; what is the warrant actually made of?
;;
;; The answer is in :warrant-provenance below and, at length, in
;; library/.spider/aif-attestation-warrant-provenance-2026-09-02.edn. All four
;; of aif's @why attestations -- including the two an owner attested -- cite as
;; their external evidence a record that is the spider's own turn-start prompt,
;; and the excerpt each one verifies against is a sentence copied out of the
;; SOURCE PATTERN FILE. The warrant doing the work is pattern text; the store
;; citation is the route it took to become admissible.
;;
;; NOTHING HERE IS AN EDGE YET, for the same reason as slice 1: an authored
;; warrant cannot currently be recorded as an attestation. See
;; library/.spider/posthoc-warrant-blocker-2026-09-02.edn and
;; holes/labs/library-contract/decisions.edn :posthoc-warrant-evidence.
{:schema :library-contract/posthoc-readings-v1
 :section "aif"
 :slice {:item :L9 :n 2 :by "claude-owner" :at "2026-09-02"
         :read "all 33 library/aif/*.flexiarg; library/aif/attestations.edn (62 rows); library/aif/.spider/absences.edn (empty vector); library/aif/.spider/seat-failures.edn (2 rows); library/aif/.spider/state.edn; library/aif/.spider/harvest-lint.edn; library/aif/proposals.edn (empty); library/aif/attestations-4d-audit.edn; library/aif/attestations-v3-reflection-audit.edn; library/.spider/harvest-verify-2026-08-30.edn; library/.spider/fleet-2026-08-30.edn; and the 56 distinct evidence records those attestations cite, fetched from the live store"}

 ;; Every one of the 33 patterns is placed in exactly one bucket below, by the
 ;; pattern taken as the SOURCE of a possible reading.
 :census {:patterns 33
          :authored-why 2                  ; grounded-actuation, posterior-variance
          :editorial-why-spelled-as-authored 4
          :proposed-posthoc 2
          :considered-not-proposed 7
          :no-reading-found 18}
 :census-note
 "Sums to 33; verified mechanically, not by eye -- every aif/*.flexiarg appears
  in exactly one bucket, with one bookkeeping exception stated here.
  aif/off-continuity-null-discriminates is bucketed under
  :editorial-why-spelled-as-authored, and a reading it is the SOURCE of also
  appears in :considered-not-proposed. So that key holds eight entries over
  seven patterns."

 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; The rule this slice selected by, stated so a reviewer can check the
 ;; selection and not only the readings.
 ;;
 ;; (1) NAMED, NOT RESEMBLING. A reading is proposed only where the source
 ;;     pattern's own prose names the target -- by wikilink, by quoting the
 ;;     target's own clause, or by using the target's claim as its premise.
 ;;     Two patterns that merely share a shape do not make an edge: that is
 ;;     inference from similarity, which P-validated-R5 law O2 refuses in the
 ;;     harvested lane and which README-flexiarg 5a does not license in the
 ;;     authored one either.
 ;; (2) THE AUTHOR TYPED THE PAIR ALREADY. Where a directive of any kind
 ;;     already joins the two patterns, in either direction, the author has
 ;;     chosen a relation for that pair. A post-hoc @why over the same pair is
 ;;     a re-typing, not a gap, and this lane does not have standing to
 ;;     overrule it. Recorded in :considered-not-proposed, not silently
 ;;     dropped.
 ;; (3) DIRECTION TOWARD THE GENERAL, as 5a has it.
 ;;
 ;; Rule (2) does most of the work in this section, which is why the yield is
 ;; 2 of 33 against slice 1's 5 of 28: wave 2 added 13 @how and 45 @see-also
 ;; edges here, so most pairs a reader would want to relate are already typed.
 :selection-rule-applied true

 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; PROPOSED. A retrospective reading with a statable warrant, direction toward
 ;; the general. Neither is a causal claim: this lane did not write either
 ;; pattern.
 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 :proposed
 [{:edge {:from "aif/two-layer-calibration"
          :to "aif/no-self-certification"
          :kind :why-posthoc}
   :rating :strong
   :warrant
   "TWO-LAYER-CALIBRATION states the dependency in its own canonical-instance paragraph -- the L1/L2 split was forced by discovering the calibration was self-certifying -- and wikilinks aif/no-self-certification as it says so. Its BECAUSE then restates no-self-certification's thesis as its own premise: the only thing that escapes prior-equals-value is a referent the model had no hand in, which is no-self-certification's conclusion with the word verdict replaced by value. The pair carries no directive in either direction."
   :warrant-pointers
   [{:at "library/aif/two-layer-calibration.flexiarg:43-44"
     :quote "The split was forced by discovering the calibration was self-certifying"}
    {:at "library/aif/two-layer-calibration.flexiarg:35"
     :quote "The only thing that escapes `prior == value` is a referent the model had no hand in."}
    {:at "library/aif/no-self-certification.flexiarg:14"
     :quote "A measurement / verdict apparatus must never be moveable by evidence it manufactured itself."}]
   :converges-with
   "library/aif/attestations.edn already carries this exact edge as a spider PROPOSAL: {:kind :why} by zai-2, 2026-08-30, :rung 2, :state :proposed -- correctly left a proposal, since checks/spider_runner.clj:165 gives the spider editor standing only. Its :cited clause is the same sentence quoted above. Two readers, one seat and one author, picked the same warrant independently; the disagreement is only about what the warrant may be called. The spider had to dress it as store evidence (e-09e5d48a, zai-2, its own turn-start prompt, whose text contains the sentence because the prompt quoted the pattern file); this lane would carry it as the pattern-file pointer it is."
   :promotion-candidate
   "As in slice 1's wr-10 case, the warrant here is the pattern's own prose stating its own causal history -- was FORCED BY discovering -- which is what 5a calls an author's claim. It is proposed as @why-posthoc because this lane did not write two-layer-calibration. A reviewer with author standing should consider a plain @why."}

  {:edge {:from "aif/valuation-reads-the-paperwork"
          :to "aif/declare-the-conditioning"
          :kind :why-posthoc}
   :rating :strong
   :warrant
   "VALUATION-READS-THE-PAPERWORK's BECAUSE is declare-the-conditioning's thesis used as a premise: value IS conditional on the situation, therefore a living document is a situation proxy, therefore record which text you conditioned on. Take the conditioning thesis away and the pattern has no argument left -- only an observation that prose edits move numbers, which is the thing it is explaining. It names declare-the-conditioning in its @references and declare-the-conditioning does not use its claim in return; the use is one-way where the reference is not. The pair carries no directive in either direction."
   :warrant-pointers
   [{:at "library/aif/valuation-reads-the-paperwork.flexiarg:25"
     :quote "Value IS conditional on the situation; a living document is a situation proxy."}
    {:at "library/aif/valuation-reads-the-paperwork.flexiarg:22"
     :quote "Persist, next to every score, the identity of the text it conditioned on"}
    {:at "library/aif/declare-the-conditioning.flexiarg:11"
     :quote "G(candidate) is a lambda — only G(candidate | situation) is a value."}
    {:at "library/aif/declare-the-conditioning.flexiarg:22"
     :quote "CONDITIONING (what situation-slice it consumed)"}]
   :note
   "Counter-consideration, stated because it is the one a reviewer should press: the two are same-mission siblings. Both cite M-evaluate-policies, futon2, 2026-07-03, as their evidence paragraph, and slice 1 refused wr-12 to wr-16 on exactly that ground. The difference is that same-day sibling patterns there shared a subject; here one uses the other's conclusion as its premise, and premise-use is asymmetric where provenance is not."}]

