   :why-not "The two @reference each other, so the reference picks no direction, and both draw their evidence paragraph from one incident, M-evaluate-policies 2026-07-03: the same 0.0 cascade placeholder appears in both. Neither uses the other's claim as a premise -- they state one instruction twice, at two scopes. A same-mission cohort produces peerage; @see-also is the honest relation and is out of this slice's scope."}

  {:edge {:from "aif/currency-before-merge" :to "aif/declare-the-conditioning" :kind :why-posthoc}
   :reading "Both are declare-what-your-number-means disciplines from the same mission, and declare-the-conditioning's three-axis declaration is the wider frame."
   :why-not "Same cohort, mutual @references, and different axes: currency-before-merge is about UNITS across lanes, declare-the-conditioning about which SITUATION-SLICE a surface consumed. Neither argument needs the other to stand."}

